WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:05.920
Speaker 1: All right. Something, something really,&nbsp;
really bad for our show happened yesterday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.920
As many of you know, we have been covering every&nbsp;
day of the Kyle Rittenhouse trial in Kenosha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:19.840
Wisconsin. And these are long days we've been&nbsp;
doing the show and streaming close to the fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.240
proceedings in court in Kenosha. I think it's an&nbsp;
important case. I think it's an interesting case.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:32.080
Somewhere between 100000 and 150000 different&nbsp;
people each day are checking out our coverage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.600
which has been on YouTube, Twitter and Facebook.&nbsp;
We have been banned by Twitch for 30 days and we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.800
have been banned by Twitch for 30 days for showing&nbsp;
something which other channels also showed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.000
including right wing channels, which I'm not&nbsp;
going to name because this isn't about getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.200
other people in trouble. And that something&nbsp;
is that yesterday, during the proceedings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.960
during the testimony of an individual named&nbsp;
Gaige Grosskreutz, an exhibit was put up by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:04.560
the prosecution, which was about eight&nbsp;
or 10 seconds of video of Grosskreutz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.840
after being shot in the bicep. And his bicep is&nbsp;
bloody. It is gory, and it was about eight or 10&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:17.200
seconds of that. We believe, because of immediate&nbsp;
reporting by what we call antagonist watchers that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:23.760
watch my stream to Twitch. Within about a minute&nbsp;
or two, our account was suspended for 30 days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:32.000
Now the reason I say it was probably because&nbsp;
of people immediately reporting us. We have a,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.720
you know, we have a close to 100000 followers&nbsp;
on Twitch. I don't or we did. I don't think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.160
Twitch is watching our stream and the fact that&nbsp;
it happened so quickly and that other channels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.280
including right wing channels who showed&nbsp;
the same video have not been banned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.240
suggests to me that was the reason. Now this&nbsp;
is I'm not going to exaggerate, but I'm not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.240
going to downplay it. This is really bad for us.&nbsp;
We've spent basically two plus years since August&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.560
of 2019 building our following on Twitch in my&nbsp;
my model of diversifying revenue streams because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.920
we've seen YouTube will take away, you know that&nbsp;
who giveth sometimes taketh away. We've lost all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.920
of our YouTube revenue for periods of a couple of&nbsp;
months. We've had issues with Facebook, et cetera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:16.640
close to 100000 followers. We had a thousand paid&nbsp;
members on Twitch because we are now suspended for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:22.720
a month. None of those thousand paid subscriptions&nbsp;
will renew. For us, a thousand paid members is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:32.640
lot. What am I doing to try to fix this? First of&nbsp;
all, let me say. I realize that. Those eight to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:39.920
10 seconds are against Twitch's guidelines&nbsp;
on gore and playing violent videos, etc..&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:47.280
We appealed the decision and said we are not&nbsp;
doing a stream of gore. We are not showing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.720
you know, these kind of violence porn videos.&nbsp;
We're showing a trial of newsworthy significance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:01.040
We're 40 hours into this trial and there were&nbsp;
eight seconds of a gory video. It is not our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:07.120
intent to broadcast gore. And it, you know,&nbsp;
there are video games with dogs being cut in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.920
half with chainsaws which are allowed now. I get&nbsp;
